{
  "kind": "classes",
  "title": "louis-agent.web.places: the interface design",
  "caption": "A site names its places once with Places(home, site); the area reads the addresses from the site's pages and its areas', the catch-all draws the page an address names, and PlaceLayout gives it that page's frame.",
